{"id":"longest-palindromic-subsequence","title":"Longest palindromic subsequence","difficulty":"medium","pattern":"reduce to LCS / interval DP","statement":"<p>Return the length of the longest subsequence of s that is a palindrome.</p>","entry":{"python":"longest_palindrome_subseq","cpp":{"name":"longestPalindromeSubseq","ret":"int","params":[["string","s"]]}},"kind":"function","compare":"exact","time_limit_ms":2000,"hints":["A palindromic subsequence of s is a common subsequence of s and reverse(s).","Or interval DP: dp[i][j] over s[i..j], matching the ends."],"complexity":"O(n\u00b2)","starter":{"python":"def longest_palindrome_subseq(s):\n    pass\n","cpp":"int longestPalindromeSubseq(string s) {\n    \n}\n"},"tests":[{"args":["bbbab"],"expected":4,"sample":true},{"args":["cbbd"],"expected":2,"sample":true},{"args":["a"],"expected":1},{"args":["abcde"],"expected":1},{"args":[""],"expected":725},{"args":[""],"expected":972}],"solution":{"explanation":"<p>Two derivations, both worth knowing: (1) <strong>reduction</strong>: LPS(s) = LCS(s, reversed s); (2) <strong>interval DP</strong>: if s[i] = s[j], dp[i][j] = 2 + dp[i+1][j\u22121], else max(dp[i+1][j], dp[i][j\u22121]), filled by increasing length. Interval DP is Part 7's first topic; this is a gentle preview.</p>","python":"def longest_palindrome_subseq(s):\n    n = len(s)\n    dp = [0] * n\n    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n        new = [0] * n\n        new[i] = 1\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            new[j] = dp[j - 1] + 2 if s[i] == s[j] else max(dp[j], new[j - 1])\n        dp = new\n    return dp[n - 1]\n","cpp":"int longestPalindromeSubseq(string s) {\n    int n = s.size(); vector<int> dp(n, 0), nw(n, 0);\n    for (int i = n - 1; i >= 0; i--) { fill(nw.begin(), nw.end(), 0); nw[i] = 1; for (int j = i + 1; j < n; j++) nw[j] = s[i] == s[j] ? dp[j-1] + 2 : max(dp[j], nw[j-1]); swap(dp, nw); }\n    return dp[n - 1];\n}\n"}}